## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where Feishu debug logs containing emoji or supplementary-plane Unicode characters (e.g. 🚨, 😀, 🎉) could produce garbled text with lone surrogates when a log message exceeds 500 code units and the truncation boundary falls in the middle of a UTF-16 surrogate pair.

This affects two log-value truncation helpers in the feishu extension:

- `sanitizeLogValue` (`card-action.ts`) — truncates chat-type resolution error messages at 500 code units
- `formatFeishuWsErrorForLog` (`monitor.transport.ts`) — truncates WebSocket error messages at `FEISHU_WS_LOG_ERROR_MAX_LENGTH` (500 code units)

These two helpers were missed in the earlier sweep (c16bb8725a) that already covered `bot.ts` and `monitor.comment.ts` in the same extension — both using the identical `truncateUtf16Safe` import from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime`.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace raw `.slice(0, N)` with the existing `truncateUtf16Safe` helper. `.slice()` operates on UTF-16 code units and can split a surrogate pair (e.g. 🚨 = `🚨`) in half, producing a lone high surrogate (`\uD83D`) that renders as �. `truncateUtf16Safe` rounds down to the nearest safe code-point boundary.

This is the same mechanical fix that was already applied to `bot.ts` (lines 1007, 1074) and `monitor.comment.ts` in the feishu extension by the prior sweep c16bb8725a. No new dependencies or behavioral changes — the import path is identical.

Risk note: log-only helpers, no user-visible message delivery surface affected. Operator-facing debug logs will see clean truncation instead of potential garbled characters.

## User Impact

No direct end-user impact — these are operator-facing log helpers. Feishu operators reading debug logs will see correctly truncated error messages instead of potentially garbled characters when emoji appear at the 500-code-unit truncation boundary.

## Evidence

**Premise — `.slice(0, 500)` cuts surrogate pairs at the boundary used by both helpers:**

Constructed a realistic log message with an emoji (🚨) positioned so its UTF-16 surrogate pair straddles the 500-code-unit boundary (first surrogate at index 499, second at index 500). `.slice(0, 500)` includes only the high surrogate, producing a lone surrogate. `truncateUtf16Safe` correctly rounds down to 499 code units.

```
$ node -e "
function hasLoneSurrogate(s) {
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    const code = s.charCodeAt(i);
    if (code >= 0xD800 && code <= 0xDBFF) {
      if (i + 1 >= s.length || s.charCodeAt(i + 1) < 0xDC00 || s.charCodeAt(i + 1) > 0xDFFF) return true;
      i++;
    } else if (code >= 0xDC00 && code <= 0xDFFF) return true;
  }
  return false;
}

const MAX = 500;
const msg = 'x'.repeat(499) + '🚨' + ' connection timeout';

console.log('BEFORE .slice(0,' + MAX + '): len=' + msg.slice(0, MAX).length + ' lone=' + hasLoneSurrogate(msg.slice(0, MAX)));
// Output: BEFORE .slice(0,500): len=500 lone=true ❌
"
```

**Negative control — old code produces garbled output, fix eliminates it:**

```
$ node --import tsx -e "
import { truncateUtf16Safe } from './src/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime.ts';

const MAX = 500;
const msg = 'x'.repeat(499) + '🚨' + ' rest of error details';
const old = msg.slice(0, MAX);         // OLD PATTERN (missed by prior sweep)
const fix = truncateUtf16Safe(msg, MAX); // NEW PATTERN (this PR)

function hasLone(str) { /* ... same as above ... */ }

console.log('OLD .slice(0,500) tail:', JSON.stringify(old.slice(-6)));
// → 'xxxxx\\ud83d'  ❌ LONE HIGH SURROGATE (garbled)

console.log('NEW truncateUtf16Safe:', fix.length);
// → 499  ✅ rounded down below surrogate pair
"
```

**Actual output demonstrating the fix in context:**

| Method | Length | Lone Surrogate | Tail | Correct? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.slice(0, 500)` (old) | 500 | true ❌ | `"xxxxx\ud83d"` | No — renders as � |
| `truncateUtf16Safe(x, 500)` (new) | 499 | false ✅ | `"xxxxxx"` | Yes — clean truncation |

**Changed files (diff):**

- `extensions/feishu/src/card-action.ts` — `sanitizeLogValue`: `.slice(0, 500)` → `truncateUtf16Safe(x, 500)`, +1 import
- `extensions/feishu/src/monitor.transport.ts` — `formatFeishuWsErrorForLog`: `.slice(0, N)` → `truncateUtf16Safe(x, N)`, +1 import

**Test run:** `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/feishu/` — passed (exit 0).

**What was not tested:** Live Feishu WebSocket error logs with emoji content across the boundary. No live Feishu credentials available in this checkout. The code change is identical to the already-shipped fix in `bot.ts` (c16bb8725a), using the same import path and helper function.

